L = np.asarray(Image.open(path).convert('L').filter(ImageFilter.GaussianBlur(8))).astype(float)\n    sub = L[win[1]:win[3], win[0]:win[2]]; y, x = np.unravel_index(np.argmax(sub), sub.shape)\n    return x + win[0], y + win[1]\n# VP windows used: 03 (420,1020,580,1160) · 04 (400,600,600,760) · 05 (380,380,640,520) · 07 (520,480,720,640)\n```\n\n## Appendix B: material boxes used for the per-material hex values\n\nBoxes are (x0, y0, x1, y1) with their class. Each box is a deliberate choice: a different box gives a slightly\ndifferent median.", "is_error": false, "tool_use_id": "toolu_015RrojFufEHkehHGmRrvP88", "type": "tool_result"}], "role": "user"}, "parentUuid": "846a367d-e8a9-4ab2-a36c-d5557268c94b", "permissionDecision": {"decision": "accept", "reasonType": "rule", "ruleSource": "cliArg", "source": "config"}, "promptId": "c53ad454-3350-48aa-919e-00238c9cb0b2", "sandboxed": false, "sessionId": "eae80a1c-be41-5f1a-858b-469afcc249da", "sourceToolAssistantUUID": "846a367d-e8a9-4ab2-a36c-d5557268c94b", "timestamp": "2026-11-15T19:18:41.687Z", "type": "user", "userType": "external", "uuid": "29d25654-8fb6-4556-906c-0b428467ce83", "version": "2.1.325"}
